KG42.register("clusters-94aac5bef8bfd6c3d471931b",{"id":"10-hierarchical_coordination::v142-d-K001","paper":"10-hierarchical_coordination","label":"Prosumer bid formation, trading roles, and curve submission","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K001","label":"Prosumer bid formation, trading roles, and curve submission","market_meaning":"Prosumers independently formulate bids based on forecast prices, scenarios, and their own supply and demand conditions, distinguish local transactions from grid transactions, comply with buying and selling role restrictions, and submit increasing supply curves or decreasing demand curves to the LMO. The submission of only one type at each time point in the case serves as a conditional procedural supplement; gaps remain in the complete stochastic optimization and the conversion from scenarios to bid blocks.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01","v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination","participation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The M01 chains jointly describe prosumer decisions and submissions in the first stage; R008 and R010 of M02 describe buying and selling roles and submission branches only at the time points in the stated case. These two scopes can be linked, but mutual exclusivity of transactions within a scenario, mutual exclusivity of submissions at a time point, and consistency of roles across scenarios cannot be directly equated.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The boundary is defined by prosumers formulating and delivering bids usable by the market, bringing together bidding, participation eligibility, product decomposition, and the receiving entity. How the LMO selects counterparties and allocates traded quantities constitutes a subsequent, separate decision. This boundary is an assembly proposal awaiting manual inspection.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the decision objective, curve constraints, and bid block structure for demand bids."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the supply offer branch and curve structure of the same prosumer decision."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Identifies the LMO as the receiving entity for both types of bid curves and retains the submission obligation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the modes of participation, grid transaction assumptions, and restrictions on buying and selling roles within scenarios."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Explains the distinction between local transaction quantities and grid transaction quantities in bids, and the decomposition of total quantities."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Adds the requirement that demand and supply submissions be mutually exclusive within the scope of the case time points."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Explains, within the scope of the case, the conditional branches under which buyers and sellers submit their corresponding curves to the LMO."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e03","v141-b-g02-e14"],"rationale":"The two chains respectively represent the demand and supply branches of the same prosumer's independent decision; citing them jointly does not mean that both types of curves must be submitted simultaneously at the same time point."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x1","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"],"rationale":"The same M01 paragraph links the monotonicity of the demand curve to submission of that curve to the LMO, connecting bid content with the submission procedure."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"],"rationale":"The same M01 paragraph links the monotonicity of the supply curve to submission of that curve to the LMO."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e14"],"rationale":"Demand bidding is a mode of participation, and restrictions on buying and selling within a scenario belong to the constraint family referenced by that decision; quantity restrictions are not rewritten as activation conditions for graph edges."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e14"],"rationale":"Supply offers and participation roles belong to the same prosumer decision; the applicability conditions of the supply branch and the existing procedural formulation in R002 are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-P-minus-jtomega","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-P-plus-jtomega"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e06"],"rationale":"The total purchase and sale quantities in the product decomposition correspond to the total quantities constrained by participation restrictions; local components and total quantities remain distinct objects and are not mapped as equal."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L07","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"The general submission procedure in M01 is illustrated concretely by the conditional branches for buyers and sellers in the M02 case; their respective source mechanisms and case limitations are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L08","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"The same case paragraph specifies both submission of only one type and the corresponding receipt procedure; the two chains jointly describe submission behavior conditional on roles."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R008::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R010::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"Both reference the existing demand submission function; the general decision and the case submission conditions are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R008::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R010::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"Both reference the existing supply submission function, without merging submission conditions of different scopes."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R010::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"The receiving entity in both chains is the LMO; node correspondence does not make the two submission edges with different conditions duplicate edges."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x1","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X002","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x1"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-en3","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e11"],"rationale":"Within the same M01, the local electricity purchase quantity for the same prosumer, time period, and scenario respectively serves the roles of bidding, submission, and a product component; differences in unit annotations are retained, and it is not equated with bid blocks indexed by m."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X001","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x2"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-en3","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e11"],"rationale":"The local electricity sale quantity in the same M01 has three local roles: bidding, submission, and a product component; each original object and its unit description are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta1","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-T001","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11"],"rationale":"The source explicitly uses the same forecast LEM price as an input to prosumer decisions and as an ordering condition for both types of curves; it is not equated with a submitted bid price or a transaction price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X002","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-O-jt"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g01-e14"],"rationale":"Both objects are the supply vector in Eq. (14), used respectively to define submission content and explain the mode of participation; differences in domain formulations are not rewritten."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O08","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"],"rationale":"The two objects duplicate the mathematical content of Eq. (13); R003 also describes submission to the LMO, so the complete constraint object and its procedural meaning are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O09","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"],"rationale":"The two objects duplicate the mathematical content of Eq. (12), while R003 additionally includes the receiving entity and the submission obligation; mathematical duplication is not used to replace the entire procedural object."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The complete prosumer optimization referenced by R001 and R002 is not fully represented within these chains. R005 already contains total purchase and sale quantities, and R007 already contains local quantities, but the grid components, complete expressions for expected costs and revenues, and the balance and flexible load objects in Eqs. (8) to (11) are still not fully represented.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e08","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e14"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream work should complete the optimization objects, constraints, and bindings based on the existing M01 evidence, or explicitly state that only an objective summary and submission rules are represented; the frozen chains are not modified in this round."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"Eqs. (12), (13) use ω for scenarios or bid blocks, while Eqs. (14), (15) use m; without an explicit conversion, scenario quantities and submitted block quantities cannot be merged item by item, nor can ordering constraints be automatically transferred to objects indexed by m.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x1","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x2","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X001","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X003","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-en2","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e12"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the index definitions, ordering conditions, and method for constructing submitted bid blocks from scenarios; keep the objects separate until an explicit correspondence is established."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G03","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The binary state in R005 is defined by time period and scenario and constrains transaction quantities; R008 and R010 constrain submission behavior at case time points. The former does not independently specify a uniform role across scenarios and cannot directly establish mutually exclusive activation of submission graph edges.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-v-jtomega","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e34"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the link between quantity decisions within scenarios and submission roles at time points, and check whether role consistency conditions exist; do not introduce a logical equivalence between binary states and graph edges."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G04","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"Objects representing the same quantity differ in whether their units are blank or marked as kWh; the nonnegative domain of the bid vector in R005 is also stronger than the direct statements in Eqs. (14), (15). These original annotations are retained, but the mapping of the same quantity in this round does not endorse their inferences about units and domains.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x1","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X002","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-B-jt","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-O-jt","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x1","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x2"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-en3","v141-b-g02-e12"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Independently check the units and the basis for the symbols, nonnegativity, and domains of each local object, then have upstream work harmonize or explain the differences."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G05","category":"unverified_source","description":"All sources in this cluster remain UNREVIEWED, with source_status=unverified; the listed mappings use only candidate evidence permitted in this round and do not indicate that the transcription or scientific content has been independently checked.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-en3","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e34"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually inspect all chains, assembly relationships, and sources; complete independent source and mathematical checks before subsequent scientific adoption."}]},"rule_refs":["10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R001","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R002","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R003","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R005","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R007","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R008","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R010"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-3fcd5e2d02ec7c3f","COMP-4fd16cbd90d234cb","COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","COMP-da34359f040da554"]});
